  "packageHash": "tIQfji4oWAskNAcJDKyrbf7g3x6afL0eHGv8t3wHIC/WzlskMTTeBwvehGh3dFnAAX+cgEXUJIqqJtkmsAM5tg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 579777,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/tree/master/src/Abblix.Jwt",
  "published": "2026-09-05T11:13:14.94Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A JWT and JOSE toolkit that uses the .NET cryptographic primitives and System.Text.Json directly, so a token round-trips with no second serializer and no key-model translation. Sign and verify with every RSA, ECDSA and HMAC algorithm of RFC 7518; encrypt with every key-management algorithm of RFC 7516, including AES key wrapping and opt-in password-based encryption with a bounded work factor; publish and consume JSON Web Keys and key sets with thumbprints and typed header accessors; process critical headers; prevent replay of single-use tokens. Keys can live outside the process: a custodian seam lets HashiCorp Vault, OpenBao Transit or Azure Key Vault hold the private half, served by the companion packages. Clock tolerance travels as one value with separate past and future halves, so a FAPI 2.0 window is expressed exactly. The token layer behind Abblix OIDC Server, usable on its own. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v2.4",
